    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9ee49f5_5c5f889c",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5711,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-27T16:08:47Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "On the dock that I am using we have the following execution path\n    DUT is SRC, dock is SNK\n    DUT sends PR_SWAP\n    dock ACCEPTS\n    DUT, new SNK, sends PS_RDY\n    dock ACCEPTS\n    dock, new SRC, sends PS_RDY\n    DUT ACCEPTS\n    dock, instead of presenting Vbus, sends HARD_RESET\n\nThis all happened after we did initial connection discovery and we are getting ready to try again with all modes exited... but PE_FLAGS_MODAL_OPERATION is set. So when we get to messages like DR_Swap, we will send a Hard Reset instead of evaluating the swap. This gets us into a loop.",
      "parentUuid": "8421213d_9991f659",
      "revId": "af9b0a2cc1217addacc81dbf5f2dc09e2984be23",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
